<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<wodefinitions>
	<wo class="WOSwitchComponent" content="allowed" unknownAttributes="forbidden">

		<doc><![CDATA[Renders a component chosen **at runtime** by name. The bound `WOComponentName` is pulled, converted to a string, and used to look up the real component (or dynamic element) via `WOApplication.dynamicElementWithName`; the request/response phases are then forwarded to that component.

Any extra attributes bound on the tag are collected and passed through as the resolved component's bindings, and the tag's content is forwarded as that component's template. Because the target name is resolved at runtime, the editor cannot know which component is being rendered — so it cannot validate those forwarded bindings, which is why the unknown-attribute policy here is `forbidden` for the switch's own API rather than passthrough.]]></doc>

		<binding name="WOComponentName" required="true">
			<pull><type>java.lang.Object</type></pull>
			<doc><![CDATA[The name of the component to render. Required. **Pulled** and read via `toString()`, so any object is accepted; if it resolves to null or empty the element renders a missing-component placeholder. This is the one binding the switch consumes itself — every other attribute on the tag is forwarded to the resolved component.]]></doc>
		</binding>

	</wo>
</wodefinitions>
